{"slug":"forza-motorsport","title":"Forza Motorsport","desc":"Xbox, Turn 10 2005 (USA)","notes":["Made with the Forza importer (import_forza.py, a Blender plugin) from the game's own car archives.  Parts are the game's own names (body, bumperFa, hooda, glassLF, headlightL, interior, wheelLF ...) as children of ONE root node named like the archive; the stock car is visible.","BODY KITS (Forza Motorsport 1 / 2 / 4, Forza Horizon): every upgrade part of the shop is in the FBX, HIDDEN, at its place on the car, in Variants/<slot> (bumperF, bumperR, skirtL, skirtR, wing, hood, cage, exhaust, trunk): the game names them <part><letter>, 'a' = stock, b .. t = the tuner kits, race = the race kit.  To see them: <car>_kits.fbx = the stock car and one complete car per kit letter (the kit's parts replace the stock ones), all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.  Variants/driver = the driver mannequin (Forza 1), Variants/popup_up = pop-up lamps up.","LODs: every lower level of detail of every part (LOD2-LOD5; Forza 4 / Horizon: LOD1-LOD5 next to the LOD0 car) is HIDDEN in LODs/LOD<n>.","Left out: skeleton, locators, blur discs.  Body paint is a run time shader in all these games: one plain red (the stock paint of the first livery in Forza Motorsport), baked ambient occlusion is NOT in the FBX (it is in the plugin and in the renders).","The front of the car is +Z like in the other games; the car stands on the ground at y = 0.","Folder names are the game's file ids (car_<id>.cab).  Paint: the first standard livery of every car.  Wheels: the stock wheel and tyre of the game (Mega.ca2) on the hub positions of the car file; brake calipers / rotors, interior and lamps from the livery atlas.","RIMS: _Rims holds every wheel style of the game (Mega.ca2, tires/art/<style>: 268), rim and tyre as two objects, in the size of the file, outer face towards +X, standing on the ground.  The picture of the rim is the game's wheel.xpr."],"tags":["forza-motorsport"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":